.TH MYSTRCPY 3
.SH NAME
mystrcpy \- copy a string into a destination buffer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include "mystrfunctions.h"
.br
.B int mystrcpy(char *dest, const char *src);
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mystrcpy
copies the string pointed to by
.I src
into the destination buffer pointed to by
.I dest
and appends the terminating null character.
.PP
The destination buffer must be large enough to hold the copied string.
If either pointer is NULL, the function returns -1.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns 0 on success, or -1 when an input pointer is NULL.
